            which verifies the properties that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
            would verify if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            was a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoid"} bimonoid
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
          %p
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/unital-comonoid.png"}/
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (coassociative coalgebras)
              A comonoid object in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/VectorSpaces"} VectorSpaces
              (with its usual
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra"} coalgebra
            %p
              (Beware though that the term “coalgebra” is overused in many ways, for instance in
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    coalgebras for endofunctor
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/coalgebras+for+endofunctor"} ?
              = succeed ".)" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coassociative+coalgebra"} coassociative coalgebra
          %p
          #InACartesianMonoidalCategory.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (cartesian comonoids)
              %br/
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              carries a
              %em unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              of a comonoid in the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
              with respect to the usual
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            %p
              Generally, every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \,\in\, \mathcal{C}
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \ast, \times)
              becomes (see also
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "cartesian+monoidal+category#ComonoidObjects"} there
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocommutative+coalgebra"} cocommutative
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  counit to be the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∃
                            %mo !
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \xrightarrow{\exists !} \ast
              %li
                %p
                  coproduct to be the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+morphism"} diagonal morphism
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi diag
                            %mi X
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} diag_X \,\colon\, X \to X \times X
            %p
              The analogous statement remains true for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} cartesian monoidal (infinity,1)-categories
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+infinity,1-category#CoalgebraObjects"} there
          %p
            Obvious as Exp.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InACartesianMonoidalCategory"}
            may be, it plays a somewhat profound role in various contexts:
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectra"} suspension
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coring+spectra"} coring spectra
              %br/
              In the case of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              or other models of classical
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              = succeed "-construction" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InACartesianMonoidalCategory"}
              implies the remarkable fact that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectra"} suspension spectra
              carry
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coring+spectrum"} coring spectrum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              via
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "suspension+spectrum#SmashMonoidalDiagonals"} smash-monoidal diagonals
            %p
